two bad batch episodes in one week was  an excellent may the fourth gift from  star wars hq and the second installment  of the disney plus series is full of fun  references from the galaxy far far away  here are the small details you may have  missed in episode 2 cut and run  in many ways the star wars universe is  actually pretty small  while there's an entire galaxy's worth  of star systems out there star wars  stories tend to revisit the same worlds  over and over  the salukimai system the setting for the  second episode of the bad batch is no  exception  die hard star wars fans probably knew  that the bad batch was headed to  seleucum before the episode even aired  at the end of the bad batch pilot hunter  tells tech to plot a course for j19  that's a designation for the sector  which contains seleumi as revealed in  the star wars the clone wars episode  grievous intrigue  in that episode the commander of the  separatist droid army general grievous  captures jedi master eth koth  and takes him to seleucum i forcing  obi-wan kenobi anakin skywalker and  master adigalia to mount a rescue  mission  the jedi save cough but grievous crash  lands on salukimi  setting up the events of the next  episode the deserter in which we meet  cut and sue for the first time  it's not the last time we'll see  selukimai in the star wars timeline  either  in revenge of the sith salukimai is  where the jedi stasa lee is killed while  on her speeder bike following the  issuing of order 66.  so cut sue and their family aren't new  characters but their family farm has a  new look  in the deserter captain rex injured in  an attack shelters with the clone  deserter and his wife  in exchange for their hospitality rex  promises not to rat cut out and leaves  them to live their lives once he's  healthy  clearly that happened a while ago  because when the bad batch reunites  viewers with a la quaine farm  things look very different cut now has a  grey streak in his hair  indicating how much he's aged his  children have grown as well  the farm itself is now surrounded by a  wire fence and other security measures  including battle droid sentries likely  cobbled together from pieces of those  destroyed during the deserter  say what you will about the empire but  if nothing else it's very efficient  presumably cut and run takes place right  after palpatine issued order 66 and  transformed the republic into the  galactic empire  jedi bodies were still being hauled out  of kamino when the bad batch returned  and they fled almost immediately  afterwards but by the time the clones  get to salukemai the imperial  machine is already up and running you  can see this best when kut and hunter  head into town to get the lay of the  land  instead of the eight-pointed emblem of  the galactic republic all government  buildings now sport the six-spoked  imperial crest  the language has been updated too the  kiosk where the clone troopers issue  chain codes and shuttle tickets has been  renamed the imperial information station  those credits won't do you any good  without a chain code  new galactic policy the imperial chain  codes that cause cut sue and the bad  batch so much  trouble are pretty new additions to star  wars canon 2. they were first mentioned  in the pilot episode of the mandalorian  and have only actually popped up on  screen  once in episode 14 of the mandalorian  boba fett shares his chain code with din  jaren in order to prove  ownership of his best gar armor the bad  batch aren't the only clones who escaped  order 66.  in the final episodes of the clone wars  series finale ahsoka tano disables clone  captain rex's inhibitor chip freeing him  from emperor palpatine's mind  control in turn rex helps ahsoka escape  the clone army and fake her death paving  the way for her return in star wars  rebels and the mandalorian  that's why when rex gets name dropped in  cut and run it's a big deal  rex is a major figure in star wars lore  not only was he anakin skywalker second  in command during the clone wars but he  ended up fighting for the rebellion  thanks to the heroes of star wars rebels  he even fought on the forced moon of  endor helping the rebels destroy the  second death star and bringing the  empire to its knees  however we know absolutely nothing about  what rex was up to between the clone  wars and star wars rebels leaving a huge  gap in his history  one that the bad batch looks like it's  going to fill not only has rex been  sighted in trailers for the bad batch  but cut and sue mentioned that the bad  batch are only a day or so behind it  expect rex to show up sooner rather than  later check out one of our newest videos  right here  plus even more looper videos about your  favorite star wars stories are coming  soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

